.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Routines for managing unsigned 128 bit integers\&. 

We do this to have a portable way on systems that have no native support\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void sc_uint128_add (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Adds the uint128_t \fIb\fP to the uint128_t \fIa\fP\&. \fIresult\fP == \fIa\fP or \fIresult\fP == \fIb\fP is not allowed\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The sum \fIa\fP + \fIb\fP will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_add_inplace (\fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b)"

.PP
Adds the uint128 \fIb\fP to the uint128_t \fIa\fP\&. The result is saved in \fIa\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. \fIa\fP will be overwritten by \fIa\fP + \fIb\fP\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_bitwise_and (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Calculates the bitwise and of the uint128_t \fIa\fP and the uint128_t \fIb\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. Furthermore, \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP and/or \fIb\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The bitwise and of \fIa\fP and \fIb\fP will be saved\&. in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_bitwise_and_inplace (\fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b)"

.PP
Calculates the bitwise and of the uint128_t \fIa\fP and the uint128_t \fIb\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The bitwise and will be saved in \fIa\fP\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_bitwise_neg (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Calculates the bitwise negation of the uint128_t \fIa\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The bitwise negation of \fIa\fP will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_bitwise_or (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Calculates the bitwise or of the uint128_t \fIa\fP and \fIb\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. Furthermore, \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP and/or \fIb\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The bitwise or of \fIa\fP and \fIb\fP will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_bitwise_or_inplace (\fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b)"

.PP
Calculates the bitwise or of the uint128_t \fIa\fP and the uint128_t \fIb\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The bitwise or will be saved in \fIa\fP\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int sc_uint128_chk_bit (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * input, int exponent)"

.PP
Returns the bit_number-th bit of \fIinput\fP\&. This function checks a bit of an existing, initialized value\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIexponent\fP The bit (counted from the right hand side) that is checked by logical and\&. Require 0 <= \fIbit_number\fP < 128\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if the checked bit is set, false if not\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int sc_uint128_compare (const void * a, const void * b)"

.PP
Compare the sc_uint128_t \fIa\fP and the sc_uint128_t \fIb\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns -1 if a < b, 1 if a > b and 0 if a == b\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_copy (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * input, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * output)"

.PP
Copies an initialized sc_uint128_t to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP A pointer to the \fBsc_uint128\fP that is copied\&. 
.br
\fIoutput\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The high and low bits of \fIoutput\fP will be set to the high and low bits of \fIinput\fP, respectively\&. 
.RE
.PP

