.RE
.PP

.SS "int sc_uint128_is_equal (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b)"

.PP
Checks if the sc_uint128_t \fIa\fP and the sc_uint128_t \fIb\fP are equal\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a true value if \fIa\fP and \fIb\fP are equal, false otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_set_bit (\fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, int exponent)"

.PP
Sets the exponent-th bit of \fIa\fP to one and keep all other bits\&. This function modifies an existing, initialized value\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIexponent\fP The bit (0-based from the rightmost bit) that is set to one by logical or\&. 0 <= \fIexponent\fP < 128\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_shift_left (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * input, int shift_count, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Calculates the bit left shift of uint128_t \fIinput\fP by shift_count bits\&. We shift in zeros from the right\&. If \fIshift_count\fP >= 128, \fIresult\fP is 0\&. All bits left from the 127th bit (counted zero based from the right hand side) drop out\&. \fIinput\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIshift_count\fP Bits to shift\&. \fIshift_count\fP >= 0\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The left shifted number will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_shift_right (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * input, int shift_count, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Calculates the bit right shift of uint128_t \fIinput\fP by shift_count bits\&. We shift in zeros from the left\&. If \fIshift_count\fP >= 128, \fIresult\fP is 0\&. All bits right from the zeroth bit (counted from the right hand side) drop out\&. \fIinput\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIshift_count\fP Bits to shift\&. \fIshift_count\fP >= 0\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The right shifted number will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_sub (const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b, \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Subtracts the uint128_t \fIb\fP from the uint128_t \fIa\fP\&. This function assumes that the result is >= 0\&. \fIresult\fP == \fIa\fP or \fIresult\fP == \fIb\fP is not allowed\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. The difference \fIa\fP - \fIb\fP will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_uint128_sub_inplace (\fBsc_uint128_t\fP * a, const \fBsc_uint128_t\fP * b)"

.PP
Subtracts the uint128_t \fIb\fP from the uint128_t \fIa\fP\&. The result is saved in \fIa\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. This function assumes that the result is >= 0\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. \fIa\fP will be overwritten by \fIa\fP - \fIb\fP\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a sc_uint128_t\&. 
.RE
.PP

